+        "description": "Certify the Forge NormalizedVizSpec returned by viz.render. Returns coverage, a measured conformant result, findings, and four pillars: a11yEquivalence, determinism, contrast and accuracy. Read-only: it reads the IR and the matching data operand without rebuilding or recommending a chart.\n\nDECLARED COVERAGE. The five Cartesian types certify from the IR alone. The eight ECharts-primary types certify under the declared operand profile when the same data branch used by viz.render is supplied. ECharts conformance requires a11yEquivalence:'pass', contrast neither 'fail' nor 'ungradeable', stable determinism, and accuracy:'pass' with rulesEvaluated > 0 and no detected distortion. A certified chart can be conformant:false; inspect the pillars and findings. No Vega-Lite compile is added to the ECharts profile. Spec-only ECharts calls remain coverage:'uncertified' with conformant:null and notes naming the missing operand. Unmodeled marks remain explicitly uncertified.\n\nDATA. An ECharts-primary IR carries metadata; nodes, links, rows and geometry live in its original branch. Supply exactly the matching hierarchy, sankey, chord, network or geo branch as data. The tool validates it against the mark trait. Data on a Cartesian IR is OODS-V123 because those charts certify from their IR. HTML or invalid IR is OODS-V126.\n\nACCESSIBILITY. The 16 equivalence rules evaluate the operand-built table and narrative. Error-severity failures fail the ECharts pillar and conformance. Warnings stay visible without failing the pillar. Findings keep their native severity. a11yNotApplicable lists rules whose declared preconditions were absent; absence is not a meaningful pass. This channel is present when the ECharts engine completed, including [] if no rule was inapplicable, and absent for spec-only, Cartesian or incomplete engine evaluations. A completed engine with an individual rule fault retains its findings and not-applicable results while failing the pillar. An